      "tool_call_id": "call_d3907f832b504726aca7bdc8",
      "name": "semantic_get",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"id\": \"FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY\", \"name\": \"FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY\", \"desc\": \"Bridge table mapping facilities organizations to their department/lab/center (DLC) keys: one row per organization-DLC key assignment. Used to filter organizations that have a non-null DLC key assignment before joining FCLT_ORGANIZATION (via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY or DLC_KEY) for DLC-level facility and room statistics.\", \"columns\": {\"FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Foreign key to FCLT_ORGANIZATION.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY identifying the organization in the DLC assignment\"}, \"DLC_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key, e.g. 'D_AEROASTRO'; joins to FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY; non-null values identify organizations with a DLC assignment\"}}}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"name\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization dimension table: one row per organization in the institute's hierarchical organization tree (levels 1-6, from institute-wide down to sub-units), with organization identifiers and names, parent and major-organization attribution, hierarchy level, assignable-space flag, course number for academic departments, description, DLC (department/lab/center) key and name, and cross-references to HR organization units. Parent of SPACE_UNIT (space assigned to organizations) and referenced by FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for room occupancy attribution.\", \"columns\": {\"FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the facilities organization; joins to SPACE_UNIT.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY and FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Organization identifier (same value as the organization key in current data)\"}, \"ORGANIZATION\": {\"desc\": \"Short organization abbreviation, e.g. 'AERO', 'ADMISS'\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Display name of the organization, e.g. 'AERO & ASTRO'; used for organization-name reporting\"}, \"FCLT_ORG_PARENT_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Key of the parent organization in the hierarchy tree; null for the top-level organization\"}, \"ORG_PARENT\": {\"desc\": \"Abbreviation of the parent organization, e.g. 'S ENG' (School of Engineering)\"}, \"FCLT_MAJOR_ORG_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Key of the major (top-level grouping) organization this organization rolls up to\"}, \"MAJOR_ORG\": {\"desc\": \"Abbreviation of the major organization, e.g. 'PROVST', 'CHNCLR'\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_LEVEL\": {\"desc\": \"Level of the organization in the hierarchy tree (1 = institute-wide root, 2-4 = intermediate divisions/schools, 5 = department/DLC level, 6 = sub-organization); stored as string, filter with values like '5'\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Official organization number used in administrative systems\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable hierarchical organization code reflecting the tree path\"}, \"ASSIGNABLE\": {\"desc\": \"Flag ('1'/'0') indicating whether the organization is an assignable-space organizational unit\"}, \"COURSE\": {\"desc\": \"Academic course (department) number for degree-granting academic departments, e.g. '16' for Aeronautics and Astronautics; null for non-academic organizations\"}, \"DESCRIPTION\": {\"desc\": \"Long description of the organization, e.g. 'Department of Aeronautics and Astronautics'; null for many non-academic organizations\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}, \"DLC_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key, e.g. 'D_AEROASTRO'; joins to FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY.DLC_KEY, HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY (for HR org unit title/level and HR department attributes; may fan out when a DLC maps to multiple HR org units), and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY (for the standard department hierarchy path)\"}, \"DLC_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center full name, e.g. 'Aeronautics and Astronautics'\"}, \"HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE_OLD\": {\"desc\": \"Legacy HR department code cross-reference\"}, \"HR_ORG_UNIT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"HR organization unit identifier cross-reference; links to HR_ORG_UNIT\"}, \"HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department name as recorded in HR systems\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per facilities organization\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_UNIT\", \"name\": \"SPACE_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"Space unit dimension table: one row per space unit (an organizational space-assignment unit such as a department, program, or office that receives space allocation), with space unit key/code, space unit name, the facilities organization it belongs to, and DLC key. Bridges FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization attribution) and SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to the space unit); used to group room counts and space statistics by space unit.\", \"columns\": {\"FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Foreign key to FCLT_ORGANIZATION.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY; the organization that owns/occupies this space unit\"}, \"SPACE_UNIT_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the space unit; joins to SPACE_DETAIL.SPACE_UNIT_KEY and SPACE_UNIT2.SPACE_UNIT_KEY; used for partitioning/ordering in space analyses\"}, \"SPACE_UNIT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Business code of the space unit (same numeric value as the key in current data)\"}, \"SPACE_UNIT\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the space unit, e.g. 'Physics', 'Technology & Policy Program'\"}, \"DLC_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key, e.g. 'D_PHYSICS'; may contain composite values like 'D_DSL:HQ'\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per space unit\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"name\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy table: one row per department/lab/center (DLC) under the 'Standard Hierarchy' hierarchy type, recording the DLC key/code/name and its five-level hierarchy path from the institute root (level 1 'All Departments') through executive areas down to the DLC's placement, with each level's code and name (null for levels deeper than the DLC's position). Joins to HR_ORG_UNIT and FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY; used to report or filter the master-hierarchy placement (school/area path) of a DLC, and as a DLC scope filter when only DLCs present in the standard hierarchy should be included.\", \"columns\": {\"HIERARCHY_TYPE\": {\"desc\": \"Hierarchy classification of the row; only 'Standard Hierarchy' exists in current data\"}, \"DLC_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key, e.g. 'D_CAMPLAN'; joins to HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY and FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY\"}, \"DLC_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center code (same value as DLC_KEY in current data); matches MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT.D_CODE\"}, \"DLC_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center full name, e.g. 'Campus Planning'\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_1_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Code of the level-1 hierarchy node, 'D_ALL' for all rows\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_1_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-1 hierarchy node, 'All Departments'\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Code of the level-2 hierarchy node, e.g. 'D_EXECVP_AREA'\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-2 hierarchy node, e.g. \\\"Executive Vice President's Area\\\"\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_3_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Code of the level-3 hierarchy node; null when the DLC's path is shallower than 3 levels\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_3_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-3 hierarchy node, e.g. 'VP Finance Area'; null for shallow paths\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_4_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Code of the level-4 hierarchy node; null for shallow paths\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_4_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-4 hierarchy node; null for shallow paths\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_5_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Code of the level-5 (deepest) hierarchy node; null for shallow paths\"}, \"MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_5_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-5 (deepest) hierarchy node; null for shallow paths\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per DLC under the standard hierarchy type\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3235\", \"name\": \"Provost Area Department Facility Organization Counts with HR Org Unit Count Dispersion\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and its corresponding facility organization key where the department is in the Provost Area, provide the number of organizations, the minimum department hierarchy level 3 code, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of HR organization units per facility organization (considering only those with a non-null DLC key and where the hierarchy type is 'Standard Hierarchy'), listing the results in order by department name and facility organization key. Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"sql\": \"WITH ProvostAreaDepts AS ( SELECT m.DLC_NAME, f.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, COUNT(f.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY) AS org_count, MIN(m.MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_3_CODE) AS min_level3_code FROM MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY m JOIN FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY f ON m.DLC_KEY = f.DLC_KEY WHERE m.MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME = 'Provost Area' GROUP BY m.DLC_NAME, f.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY ), FacilityOrgStats AS ( SELECT f.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, MAX(hr_unit_count) - MIN(hr_unit_count) AS org_unit_count_range, VARIANCE(hr_unit_count) AS org_unit_count_variance, STDDEV(hr_unit_count) AS org_unit_count_stddev FROM FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY f JOIN MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY m ON f.DLC_KEY = m.DLC_KEY JOIN ( SELECT h.DLC_KEY, COUNT(*) AS hr_unit_count FROM HR_ORG_UNIT h WHERE h.DLC_KEY IS NOT NULL GROUP BY h.DLC_KEY ) AS hr_stats ON m.DLC_KEY = hr_stats.DLC_KEY WHERE f.DLC_KEY IS NOT NULL AND m.HIERARCHY_TYPE = 'Standard Hierarchy' GROUP BY f.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY ORDER BY org_unit_count_range DESC ), CombinedProvostFacility AS ( SELECT p.DLC_NAME, p.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, p.org_count, p.min_level3_code, f.org_unit_count_range, f.org_unit_count_variance, f.org_unit_count_stddev FROM ProvostAreaDepts p JOIN FacilityOrgStats f ON p.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY = f.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY ) SELECT * FROM CombinedProvostFacility ORDER BY DLC_NAME, FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY;\", \"category\": \"Facility Space and Organization Hierarchy Comprehensive Analysis\", \"default_granularity\": \"one row per Provost Area department name and facility organization key with HR org unit count dispersion statistics\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2559\", \"name\": \"Office-Named DLCs with Assignable Organization Counts, Provost Area Department Max Organization Number, Space Unit, and Earliest Load Date\", \"desc\": \"For each DLC whose DLC name contains the word 'Office', is not the biology department, and has at least one assignable organization, what are the DLC key, DLC name, the number of unique organizations, the total number of assignable organizations, the department name, the maximum organization number, the name of the space unit associated with that department, and the earliest warehouse load date among its organizations, considering only departments in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" with a maximum organization number greater than 50000 and excluding the \\\"Political Science\\\" department (Course 17)? Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"sql\": \"WITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT d.DLC_KEY, o.DLC_NAME, COUNT(DISTINCT o.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY) AS organization_count, SUM(CASE WHEN o.ASSIGNABLE = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS assignable_organization_count FROM FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY d JOIN FCLT_ORGANIZATION o ON d.DLC_KEY = o.DLC_KEY WHERE o.ASSIGNABLE = 1 AND o.DLC_NAME LIKE '%Office%' AND LOWER(o.DLC_NAME) != LOWER('Biology') GROUP BY d.DLC_KEY, o.DLC_NAME ), Dept_Max_Org_Space AS ( SELECT mdh.DLC_KEY, mdh.DLC_NAME AS department, MAX(fo.ORGANIZATION_NUMBER) AS max_organization_number, su.SPACE_UNIT AS space_unit_name FROM MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY mdh JOIN FCLT_ORGANIZATION fo ON mdh.DLC_KEY = fo.DLC_KEY LEFT JOIN SPACE_UNIT su ON fo.DLC_KEY = su.DLC_KEY WHERE mdh.MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME = 'Provost Area' AND fo.ORGANIZATION_NUMBER > 50000 AND mdh.DLC_NAME <> 'Political Science' GROUP BY mdh.DLC_KEY, mdh.DLC_NAME, su.SPACE_UNIT ), Org_Earliest_Load AS ( SELECT o.DLC_KEY, MIN(o.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE) AS earliest_warehouse_load_date FROM FCLT_ORGANIZATION o GROUP BY o.DLC_KEY ) SELECT ic.DLC_KEY, ic.DLC_NAME, ic.organization_count, ic.assignable_organization_count, dmos.department, dmos.max_organization_number, dmos.space_unit_name, oel.earliest_warehouse_load_date FROM inner_cte ic JOIN Dept_Max_Org_Space dmos ON ic.DLC_KEY = dmos.DLC_KEY LEFT JOIN Org_Earliest_Load oel ON ic.DLC_KEY = oel.DLC_KEY;\", \"category\": \"Facility Space and Organization Hierarchy Comprehensive Analysis\", \"default_granularity\": \"one row per Office-named DLC matched with Provost Area department space unit and load date statistics\"}], \"not_found\": []}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_6eaad2546d0e43598bfa2a3e",
      "name": "semantic_get",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"default_granularity\": \"one row per large space unit matched with its Provost Area HR department rank\", \"desc\": \"For each space unit with a space unit key greater than 100000 that is associated with a department in the \\\"Provost Area\\\", show the space unit code, the organization name, the HR department name, the sum of space unit keys within each warehouse load date group, the HR department code, the school area name, and the rank of the department within its school area based on department code. Present the results ordered by school area name, department rank within school area, and space unit code. Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"id\": \"dw_3342\", \"name\": \"Large Space Units with Provost Area Department School-Area Ranks and Load-Date Key Sums\", \"sql\": \"WITH ProvostDepartments AS ( SELECT t1.HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE, t1.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, t1.ORG_HIER_SCHOOL_AREA_NAME, RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t1.ORG_HIER_SCHOOL_AREA_NAME ORDER BY t1.HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE) AS window_column FROM MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY t0 INNER JOIN HR_ORG_UNIT t1 ON t0.DLC_KEY = t1.DLC_KEY WHERE t0.MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME = 'Provost Area' ), LargeSpaceUnits AS ( SELECT t0.SPACE_UNIT_CODE, t1.ORGANIZATION_NAME, t2.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, SUM(t0.SPACE_UNIT_KEY) OVER (PARTITION BY t0.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE ORDER BY t0.SPACE_UNIT_KEY) AS window_column, t2.HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE FROM SPACE_UNIT t0 JOIN FCLT_ORGANIZATION t1 ON t0.DLC_KEY = t1.DLC_KEY JOIN HR_ORG_UNIT t2 ON t1.DLC_KEY = t2.DLC_KEY WHERE t0.SPACE_UNIT_KEY > 100000 ) SELECT lsu.SPACE_UNIT_CODE, lsu.ORGANIZATION_NAME, lsu.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, lsu.window_column AS space_unit_sum_within_load_date, pd.HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE, pd.ORG_HIER_SCHOOL_AREA_NAME, pd.window_column AS department_rank_within_school_area FROM LargeSpaceUnits lsu JOIN ProvostDepartments pd ON lsu.HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE = pd.HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE ORDER BY pd.ORG_HIER_SCHOOL_AREA_NAME, pd.window_column, lsu.SPACE_UNIT_CODE;\", \"category\": \"Facility Space and Organization Hierarchy Comprehensive Analysis\"}, {\"default_granularity\": \"one row per Provost Area department hierarchy row matched with a large space unit of the same DLC\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" with a non-null department code, show the department name, the department's long name, the corresponding hierarchy level 3 name from the master department hierarchy, the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the department name, and for each matching space unit with a space unit key greater than 100000, show the space unit code, the organization name, the HR department name from the space unit, and the sum of space unit keys within each warehouse load date group ordered by space unit key. Present the results ordered by department name and space unit code. Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"id\": \"dw_3490\", \"name\": \"Provost Area Department Hierarchy Windows Matched with Large Space Unit Load-Date Key Sums\", \"sql\": \"WITH DeptWindowed AS ( SELECT t1.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, t1.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME_LONG, t0.MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_3_NAME, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY t1.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING) AS window_column, t1.DLC_KEY FROM MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY t0 JOIN HR_ORG_UNIT t1 ON t0.DLC_KEY = t1.DLC_KEY WHERE t1.ORG_HIER_TOP_LEVEL_NAME = 'Provost Area' AND t1.HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE IS NOT NULL ), SpaceUnitWindowed AS ( SELECT t0.SPACE_UNIT_CODE, t1.ORGANIZATION_NAME, t2.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, SUM(t0.SPACE_UNIT_KEY) OVER (PARTITION BY t0.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE ORDER BY t0.SPACE_UNIT_KEY) AS window_column, t2.DLC_KEY FROM SPACE_UNIT t0 JOIN FCLT_ORGANIZATION t1 ON t0.DLC_KEY = t1.DLC_KEY JOIN HR_ORG_UNIT t2 ON t1.DLC_KEY = t2.DLC_KEY WHERE t0.SPACE_UNIT_KEY > 100000 ) SELECT d.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, d.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME_LONG, d.MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_3_NAME, d.window_column AS dept_window_column, s.SPACE_UNIT_CODE, s.ORGANIZATION_NAME, s.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME AS spaceunit_hr_department_name, s.window_column AS spaceunit_window_column FROM DeptWindowed d JOIN SpaceUnitWindowed s ON d.DLC_KEY = s.DLC_KEY ORDER BY d.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, s.SPACE_UNIT_CODE\", \"category\": \"Facility Space and Organization Hierarchy Comprehensive Analysis\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1864\", \"name\": \"Level-5 Assignable Organization Space Units with Provost Area HR Department Statistics\", \"desc\": \"For each organization whose organization level is 5 and is not 'ADMISSIONS', and for each organization and its corresponding HR department where the organization is assignable, the HR organization unit level is 'DEPARTMENTS', the organization is not 'Cambridge-MIT Institute', and the organization is in the 'Provost Area' top-level HR hierarchy, but excluding organizations with organization IDs '138' and '250', show the organization name, description, the corresponding space unit name, the total number of space units associated with each organization, the HR department name, the number of organizations, and the minimum organization number. Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"sql\": \"WITH org_space_units AS ( SELECT ORGANIZATION_NAME, DESCRIPTION, SPACE_UNIT, COUNT(SPACE_UNIT) OVER (PARTITION BY ORGANIZATION_NAME) AS total_space_units, DLC_KEY FROM ( SELECT t0.ORGANIZATION_NAME, t0.DESCRIPTION, t1.SPACE_UNIT, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY t1.SPACE_UNIT ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING) AS window_column, t0.DLC_KEY FROM FCLT_ORGANIZATION t0 JOIN SPACE_UNIT t1 ON t0.DLC_KEY = t1.DLC_KEY WHERE t0.ORGANIZATION_LEVEL = 5 AND t0.ORGANIZATION_NAME <> 'ADMISSIONS' AND t0.ORGANIZATION_ID NOT IN ('138', '250') ) inner_cte ), org_hr_dept AS ( SELECT ic.ORGANIZATION, ic.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, ic.organization_count, ic.min_organization_number, f.DLC_KEY FROM ( SELECT f.ORGANIZATION, h.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, COUNT(f.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY) AS organization_count, MIN(f.ORGANIZATION_NUMBER) AS min_organization_number FROM FCLT_ORGANIZATION f JOIN HR_ORG_UNIT h ON f.HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE_OLD = h.HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE_OLD WHERE f.ASSIGNABLE = 1 AND h.HR_ORG_UNIT_LEVEL = 'DEPARTMENTS' AND f.ORGANIZATION_NAME NOT IN ('CAMBRIDGE-MIT INST') AND f.ORGANIZATION_ID NOT IN ('138', '250') GROUP BY f.ORGANIZATION, h.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME ) ic JOIN HR_ORG_UNIT h2 ON ic.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME = h2.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME JOIN FCLT_ORGANIZATION f ON ic.ORGANIZATION = f.ORGANIZATION WHERE h2.ORG_HIER_TOP_LEVEL_NAME = 'Provost Area' ) SELECT osu.ORGANIZATION_NAME, osu.DESCRIPTION, osu.SPACE_UNIT, osu.total_space_units, ohd.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, ohd.organization_count, ohd.min_organization_number FROM org_space_units osu JOIN org_hr_dept ohd ON osu.DLC_KEY = ohd.DLC_KEY;\", \"category\": \"Facility Space and Organization Hierarchy Comprehensive Analysis\", \"default_granularity\": \"one row per level-5 organization space unit matched with its Provost Area HR department statistics\"}, {\"default_granularity\": \"one row per assignable organization with high HR department id matched with a space-unit-code-97500 space unit row of the same organization\", \"desc\": \"For each organization that is assignable and has a department code above 100000, and for which there exists a space unit with space unit code equal to 97500, show the organization key, organization name, department name, the number of HR org units, the total of their department IDs, the latest warehouse load date from HR_ORG_UNIT, the space unit name, the DLC name, the DLC key from the organization, the minimum space unit code in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the facility organization key, and the total number of space units per organization, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"id\": \"dw_4330\", \"name\": \"Assignable Organizations with High HR Department IDs Matched with Space Unit 97500 Window Statistics\", \"sql\": \"WITH org_hr_stats AS ( WITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT f.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, f.ORGANIZATION_NAME, h.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, COUNT(h.HR_ORG_UNIT_KEY) AS hr_org_unit_count, SUM(h.HR_DEPARTMENT_ID) AS total_department_id FROM FCLT_ORGANIZATION f JOIN HR_ORG_UNIT h ON f.HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE_OLD = h.HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE_OLD WHERE f.ASSIGNABLE = 1 AND h.HR_DEPARTMENT_ID > 100000 GROUP BY f.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, f.ORGANIZATION_NAME, h.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME ) SELECT i.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, i.ORGANIZATION_NAME, i.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, i.hr_org_unit_count, i.total_department_id, MAX(h.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE) AS latest_hr_org_unit_load_date FROM inner_cte i JOIN HR_ORG_UNIT h ON i.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME = h.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME GROUP BY i.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, i.ORGANIZATION_NAME, i.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, i.hr_org_unit_count, i.total_department_id ), space_unit_stats AS ( WITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT t2.SPACE_UNIT AS space_unit_name, t1.ORGANIZATION_NAME AS organization_name, t1.DLC_NAME AS dlc_name, t1.DLC_KEY AS org_dlc_key, MIN(t2.SPACE_UNIT_CODE) OVER (ORDER BY t2.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING) AS window_min_space_unit_code, t1.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY FROM FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY t0 JOIN FCLT_ORGANIZATION t1 ON t0.DLC_KEY = t1.DLC_KEY JOIN SPACE_UNIT t2 ON t1.DLC_KEY = t2.DLC_KEY WHERE t2.SPACE_UNIT_CODE = 97500 ) SELECT inner_cte.space_unit_name, inner_cte.organization_name, inner_cte.dlc_name, inner_cte.org_dlc_key, inner_cte.window_min_space_unit_code, org_unit_counts.total_space_units, inner_cte.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY FROM inner_cte JOIN ( SELECT t1.ORGANIZATION_NAME, COUNT(DISTINCT t2.SPACE_UNIT_KEY) AS total_space_units FROM FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY t0 JOIN FCLT_ORGANIZATION t1 ON t0.DLC_KEY = t1.DLC_KEY JOIN SPACE_UNIT t2 ON t1.DLC_KEY = t2.DLC_KEY GROUP BY t1.ORGANIZATION_NAME ) AS org_unit_counts ON inner_cte.organization_name = org_unit_counts.ORGANIZATION_NAME ) SELECT o.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, o.ORGANIZATION_NAME, o.HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME, o.hr_org_unit_count, o.total_department_id, o.latest_hr_org_unit_load_date, s.space_unit_name, s.dlc_name, s.org_dlc_key, s.window_min_space_unit_code, s.total_space_units FROM org_hr_stats o JOIN space_unit_stats s ON o.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY = s.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\", \"category\": \"Facility Space and Organization Hierarchy Comprehensive Analysis\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy\", \"name\": \"Department and HR Organization Hierarchy\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing the institute's department/lab/center (DLC) and HR organization hierarchies: the HR organization unit dimension in two feed variants (HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW), the master department standard hierarchy path (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY), its DLC-to-administrative-object link table (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS), and the direct-parent department lookup (MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT). They jointly answer questions about which HR department/area a DLC or organization belongs to, the hierarchy path or parent of a department, and HR department names/codes/levels, and are joined to FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY for facilities/space attribution. They differ in hierarchy representation (full path vs direct parent vs HR unit attributes), unit coverage, and companion columns.\", \"tables\": [\"HR_ORG_UNIT\", \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\", \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS\", \"MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Granularity and business object\", \"detail\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT and HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW hold one row per HR organization unit (641 and 691 rows respectively); MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY holds one row per DLC (310 rows) with its 5-level standard hierarchy path; MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS holds one row per DLC-to-linked-object association (fund centers, profit centers, facilities orgs, org units); MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT holds one row per department code with only its direct parent.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Hierarchy representation\", \"detail\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT carries the HR hierarchy path levels 1-7 plus school-area/top-level/root names and a unit level classification (ALL MIT, TOP LEVEL, DEPARTMENTS, SUB DEPARTMENT, ORGANIZATION LEVEL, NON HIERARCHY ORG UNITS); HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW carries only levels 1-5; MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY carries the master standard-hierarchy path levels 1-5 by code and name; MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT carries no path, only the immediate parent code/name.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Coverage and feed differences\", \"detail\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW is the newer feed with more units (691 vs 641, including 50 units absent from HR_ORG_UNIT) but lacks HR_DEPARTMENT_ID, DLC_NAME, and hierarchy levels 6-7, and adds HR_DEPARTMENT_ABBR; HR_ORG_UNIT is required when DLC_NAME or the deeper path is needed. MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY covers only DLCs placed in the 'Standard Hierarchy'; MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT covers 340 department codes including some outside that hierarchy.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"DLC cross-reference columns\", \"detail\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT carries DLC_KEY and DLC_NAME (DLC_KEY null for 133 units, and one DLC_KEY may map to multiple HR unit rows); HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW carries only DLC_KEY (possibly composite like 'D_DSL:HQ'); MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS carry DLC_KEY/DLC_CODE as their primary DLC identity; MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT uses D_CODE/D_NAME naming for the same value domain.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Companion attributes\", \"detail\": \"Only the HR_ORG_UNIT tables carry HR department identifiers/codes (HR_ORG_UNIT_ID, HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE 'HR-NNNNNN', HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE_OLD) and department name variants (short/long/alpha) used for HR department reporting; only MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS carries linked administrative object keys/codes and link type classification.\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"HR org unit title, HR org unit level, HR department name/code/long name for a facilities organization or DLC\": \"Use HR_ORG_UNIT joined via DLC_KEY; it is the only table carrying DLC_NAME alongside the HR department attributes and the full levels 1-7 path.\", \"HR department attributes for units missing from the older feed, or when the newer unit coverage is required\": \"Use HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW; it holds 50 units absent from HR_ORG_UNIT but lacks DLC_NAME and hierarchy levels 6-7.\", \"School/area placement or full standard-hierarchy path of a DLC, or restricting analysis to DLCs in the standard hierarchy\": \"Use MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY (levels 1-5 codes and names per DLC).\", \"Fund center, profit center, facilities organization, or other administrative object linked to a DLC\": \"Use MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS filtered by LINK_TYPE_CODE (FC, PMIT, FORG, ORG2, ORGU, SIS, BAG).\", \"Direct parent department of a department code (single-level parent lookup)\": \"Use MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT (PARENT_D_CODE/PARENT_D_NAME); use MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY instead when the multi-level path is needed.\"}}, {\"id\": \"concept_space_unit_dimension\", \"name\": \"Space Unit Dimension\", \"desc\": \"Space unit lookup tables identifying the organizational units that receive space allocation: SPACE_UNIT (with FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY organization attribution) and SPACE_UNIT2 (identity/name only). They answer the same space-unit identity questions but differ in organization linkage and coverage.\", \"tables\": [\"SPACE_UNIT\", \"SPACE_UNIT2\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Organization attribution\", \"differences\": \"SPACE_UNIT carries FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY linking each space unit to its owning organization in FCLT_ORGANIZATION; SPACE_UNIT2 has no organization key, only space unit identity and DLC_KEY.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Coverage\", \"differences\": \"SPACE_UNIT holds more space units (150 rows) than SPACE_UNIT2 (139 rows); every SPACE_UNIT2 key also exists in SPACE_UNIT, so SPACE_UNIT2 is a subset.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Join role\", \"differences\": \"Both join SPACE_DETAIL via SPACE_UNIT_KEY; only SPACE_UNIT can bridge SPACE_DETAIL rooms to organization attributes (level, parent, description).\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Space unit analysis that needs organization attributes (organization level, name, description)\": \"Use SPACE_UNIT: it is the only space unit table carrying FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for the organization join.\", \"Space unit name/code lookup only, or queries restricted to the SPACE_UNIT2 subset\": \"Use SPACE_UNIT2: it provides SPACE_UNIT_KEY/CODE/NAME and DLC_KEY without organization linkage.\", \"Counting rooms per space unit or ranking space units by room count\": \"Join SPACE_DETAIL to SPACE_UNIT on SPACE_UNIT_KEY (preferred for full coverage and organization attribution).\"}}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_dlc_key\", \"name\": \"DLC Key (Department/Lab/Center)\", \"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key columns (values like 'D_AEROASTRO', 'D_IDSS', 'D_BIOLOGY') identifying a DLC across the facilities, HR, space, and academic-department domains. They are the universal cross-domain join key linking facilities organizations and space units to HR organization units, the master department hierarchy, and academic departments. Naming and completeness vary: DLC_KEY in most tables, D_CODE in MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, DLC_CODE in the master hierarchy tables; some columns carry composite values ('D_DSL:HQ') or nulls.\", \"columns\": [\"FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY\", \"FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY.DLC_KEY\", \"HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY\", \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW.DLC_KEY\", \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY\", \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS.DLC_KEY\", \"MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT.D_CODE\", \"SPACE_UNIT.DLC_KEY\", \"SPACE_UNIT2.DLC_KEY\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT.DLC_KEY\", \"SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE.DEPT_NAMES\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Naming convention\", \"detail\": \"DLC_KEY is used by FCLT_ORGANIZATION, FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY, HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW, MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY, MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS, SPACE_UNIT, SPACE_UNIT2, and SIS_DEPARTMENT; MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT names the same value domain D_CODE (with PARENT_D_CODE for the parent); MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY/LINKS additionally carry DLC_CODE holding the same value as DLC_KEY; SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE names it DEPT_NAMES despite holding DLC key values, not department names.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Uniqueness and fan-out behavior\", \"detail\": \"In MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY the DLC_KEY is unique per DLC (one row per DLC); in HR_ORG_UNIT one DLC_KEY may appear on multiple HR org unit rows (join fans out); in FCLT_ORGANIZATION multiple organizations can share a DLC_KEY; in FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY it is an assignment bridge where non-null values mark organizations with a DLC assignment; in SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE multiple supervisors can share the same DEPT_NAMES value, so joining DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY fans out on both sides.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Nullability and value format\", \"detail\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY is null for units without a DLC assignment (133 of 641 rows); HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW.DLC_KEY and SPACE_UNIT.DLC_KEY may contain composite values like 'D_DSL:HQ' that do not match plain DLC keys; SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE.DEPT_NAMES holds a comma-separated list of DLC keys when DEPT_COUNT > 1 (e.g. 'D_IDSS,D_LIDS'), so only single-department rows match a plain DLC key join; SIS_DEPARTMENT.DLC_KEY is populated for all 122 department rows.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Companion name column\", \"detail\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION, HR_ORG_UNIT, and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY carry a DLC_NAME alongside the key; SPACE_UNIT/SPACE_UNIT2, FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW, SIS_DEPARTMENT, and SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE carry only the key, so DLC name reporting requires joining one of the name-carrying tables.\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Attaching HR department attributes (unit title, department name/code, level) to a facilities organization\": \"Join FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY = HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY; expect possible row fan-out when a DLC maps to multiple HR org units.\", \"Reporting the DLC name of an organization or space unit\": \"Use FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY (carries DLC_NAME) or join HR_ORG_UNIT/MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY for DLC_NAME; SPACE_UNIT/SPACE_UNIT2 keys alone have no name column.\", \"Restricting analysis to DLCs placed in the standard department hierarchy or reporting their hierarchy path\": \"Join on MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY; use MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT.D_CODE for the same value domain when only the direct parent is needed.\", \"Filtering organizations that have a DLC assignment before DLC-level room statistics\": \"Use FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY.DLC_KEY IS NOT NULL as the assignment filter, then join FCLT_ORGANIZATION.\", \"Linking an academic department to its facilities organization or HR unit\": \"Use SIS_DEPARTMENT.DLC_KEY = FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY (or HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY); all SIS_DEPARTMENT rows carry a DLC key.\", \"Attributing supervisor space-usage statistics (supervisees, square footage, research volume) to a DLC or space unit\": \"Join SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE.DEPT_NAMES = SPACE_UNIT.DLC_KEY (or another DLC_KEY column); despite its name, DEPT_NAMES holds DLC key values, and only single-department rows (DEPT_COUNT = 1) match a plain DLC key.\"}}, {\"columns\": [\"FCLT_ORGANIZATION.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\", \"SPACE_UNIT.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\", \"FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\", \"FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_MINOR_ORGANIZATION_KEY\", \"FAC_ORGANIZATION.ORGANIZATION_KEY\", \"FAC_ROOMS.ORGANIZATION_KEY\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Key family\", \"differences\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY (FCLT_* family) and ORGANIZATION_KEY (FAC_* family) share the same value domain but must be joined within their own family: SPACE_UNIT/FCLT_ROOMS use FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, FAC_ROOMS uses ORGANIZATION_KEY.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Primary vs secondary occupancy\", \"differences\": \"FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY is the primary occupying organization; FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_MINOR_ORGANIZATION_KEY is the secondary organization, both referencing FCLT_ORGANIZATION.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Dimension vs foreign key\", \"differences\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY and FAC_ORGANIZATION.ORGANIZATION_KEY are dimension identities; the others are foreign keys attributing space units or rooms to organizations.\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Attributing space units to organizations (e.g. filtering by organization level)\": \"Join SPACE_UNIT.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY to FCLT_ORGANIZATION.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY.\", \"Attributing rooms to their occupying organization in the FCLT_* family\": \"Use FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY (primary) or FCLT_MINOR_ORGANIZATION_KEY (secondary) against FCLT_ORGANIZATION.\", \"Room organization attribution inside the FAC_* family\": \"Use FAC_ROOMS.ORGANIZATION_KEY against FAC_ORGANIZATION.ORGANIZATION_KEY.\"}, \"desc\": \"Facility organization key columns attributing space units and rooms to organizations in the hierarchical organization tree. Two naming conventions exist across table families (FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY in FCLT_*/SPACE_* tables vs ORGANIZATION_KEY in FAC_* tables) with the same value domain.\", \"id\": \"column_concept_facility_organization_key\", \"name\": \"Facility Organization Key\"}, {\"columns\": [\"SPACE_UNIT.SPACE_UNIT_KEY\", \"SPACE_UNIT2.SPACE_UNIT_KEY\", \"SPACE_DETAIL.SPACE_UNIT_KEY\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Role\", \"differences\": \"In SPACE_UNIT and SPACE_UNIT2 it is the primary identity of the space unit dimension; in SPACE_DETAIL it is a foreign key assigning each room to a space unit.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Organization linkage\", \"differences\": \"Only SPACE_UNIT.SPACE_UNIT_KEY rows carry FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, so joining SPACE_DETAIL through SPACE_UNIT (not SPACE_UNIT2) reaches organization attributes.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Coverage\", \"differences\": \"SPACE_DETAIL references 66 distinct space unit keys; SPACE_UNIT covers all of them plus unused units, SPACE_UNIT2 is a subset of SPACE_UNIT.\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Grouping room counts by space unit with organization attributes\": \"Join SPACE_DETAIL.SPACE_UNIT_KEY to SPACE_UNIT.SPACE_UNIT_KEY, then to FCLT_ORGANIZATION via SPACE_UNIT.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY.\", \"Space unit name lookup without organization context\": \"Either SPACE_UNIT or SPACE_UNIT2 resolves SPACE_DETAIL.SPACE_UNIT_KEY to a name; prefer SPACE_UNIT for full coverage.\"}, \"desc\": \"Space unit key columns identifying the organizational space-assignment unit across the space dimension and fact tables. SPACE_UNIT_KEY is the join key linking SPACE_DETAIL room rows to space unit identity (name/code) and, through SPACE_UNIT, to the owning facilities organization.\", \"id\": \"column_concept_space_unit_key\", \"name\": \"Space Unit Key\"}], \"not_found\": []}"
    },
